  "query_preview": "/Monday through Friday/...A ridge will remain over \nthe Four Corners region with continued hot temperatures and \nsouthwest flow over the area. A shortwave will move across the \narea on Monday morning as monsoonal moisture increases from the \nsouth. A 20-40 percent chance of thunderstorms on Monday morning\ninto the afternoon as this feature moves across eastern OR and \nsouthwest ID. Current forecast does not have this handled well, \nbut should come into better agreement as the meso models come \ninto focus. Residual moisture continues into Tuesday with a \nchance of thunderstorms on the Idaho side. Westerly flow shunts \nthe moisture to the east on Wednesday and Thursday with dry and \nbreezy conditions and slightly cooler temperatures. Temperatures\nMonday through Wednesday around 5- 10 degrees above normal \ncooling to near normal on Thursday and Friday.",
